{"content":[{"id":"7154e9b9","settings":{"content_width":"boxed","boxed_width":{"size":900,"unit":"px","sizes":[]},"padding":{"top":0,"right":0,"bottom":0,"left":0,"unit":"px","isLinked":true}},"elements":[{"id":"44e91497","settings":{"design_skin":"editorial","uf_eyebrow":"FIELD NOTES \/ 01","title":"A garden that grows with you.","title_tag":"h3","content_source":"editor","editor_content":"<p>Good gardens begin with listening. To the light moving across a wall, to the rain finding its way through the soil, to the way a family spends an ordinary afternoon.<\/p><p>We start with a simple conversation about what you want to make space for. A shady place to read. A table that fits everyone. A path that invites you outside, even on the busiest day.<\/p><p>The planting comes next: layers of texture, seasonal colour and resilient species chosen for your particular patch of ground. As the garden settles in, it becomes less like a project and more like a familiar friend.<\/p>","collapsed_height":{"size":170,"unit":"px","sizes":[]},"collapsed_height_mobile":{"size":190,"unit":"px","sizes":[]},"initial_state":"folded","unfold_duration":420,"expand_label":"Continue reading","collapse_label":"Show less","trigger":"click","show_button":"yes","show_overlay":"yes","hide_trigger_if_fits":"yes","uf_accent":"#473d2d","uf_focus":"#473d2d","box_padding":{"top":42,"right":44,"bottom":42,"left":44,"unit":"px","isLinked":false},"box_padding_mobile":{"top":28,"right":24,"bottom":28,"left":24,"unit":"px","isLinked":false},"box_gap":{"size":22,"unit":"px","sizes":[]},"title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Georgia","title_typography_font_size":{"size":42,"unit":"px","sizes":[]},"title_typography_font_size_mobile":{"size":29,"unit":"px","sizes":[]},"title_typography_font_weight":"500","title_typography_line_height":{"size":1.12,"unit":"em","sizes":[]},"content_typography_typography":"custom","content_typography_font_family":"Arial","content_typography_font_size"